From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jim Martin <jimmartin@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 13:55:28 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] phy: qcom: qmp-combo: Let the Glymur DP lane pair follow the
 orientation

On the Glymur USB43DP PHY the DP TX blocks are the USB3 lane blocks, and
the block USB3 occupies follows the cable orientation: block A in normal
and block B in reverse orientation, as selected through
QPHY_V3_DP_COM_TYPEC_CTRL. "phy: qualcomm: qmp-combo: Add
hardware-specific DP PHY config fields" sets dp_mode_ignore_reverse for
Glymur, which keeps the DP PCS on lanes 2/3 (DP_PHY_MODE 0x5c) in both
orientations. In reverse orientation the DP PCS then drives the lane pair
that carries the live USB3 link, while the DP lane table and the
driver-enable and bias settings of qmp_v8_configure_dp_phy() go to the
other block. On a Surface Laptop 8 every reverse-orientation plug of a
USB-C DisplayPort sink failed link training with USB3 unaffected, and
every normal-orientation plug worked.

Clear dp_mode_ignore_reverse for Glymur so that the DP PCS lane pair
follows the orientation as on the other QMP combo PHYs: lanes 0/1
(block A, DP_PHY_MODE 0x4c) in reverse and lanes 2/3 (block B, 0x5c) in
normal orientation. This matches the lane block that
qmp_combo_dp_lane_blocks() gives DP and the orientation-dependent
driver-enable and bias selection in qmp_v8_configure_dp_phy().

Assisted-by: Opus 5.5
Signed-off-by: Jim Martin <jimmartin@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-combo.c | 8 ++++----
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-combo.c b/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-combo.c
index be32e69b641..7d0272fdd7b 100644
--- a/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-combo.c
+++ b/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-combo.c
@@ -3499,7 +3499,6 @@ static const struct qmp_phy_cfg glymur_usb3dpphy_cfg = {
 
 	.dp_aux_cfg2		= QSERDES_DP_PHY_AUX_CFG2_V8,
 	.dp_phy_cfg1		= QSERDES_DP_PHY_CFG1_V8,
-	.dp_mode_ignore_reverse	= true,
 	.dp_lanes_exclusive	= true,
 
 	.regs			= qmp_v8_n3_usb43dpphy_regs_layout,
@@ -3520,9 +3519,10 @@ static const struct qmp_phy_cfg glymur_usb3dpphy_cfg = {
  * only the block that carries its lanes while USB3 shares the port (USB3DP
  * mode, DP on two or one lanes).  The block USB3 occupies follows the cable
  * orientation (block A in normal, block B in reverse orientation), so DP
- * takes the other one: block B in normal, block A in reverse.  This is
- * independent of dp_mode_ignore_reverse, which only concerns the DP PCS's
- * own lane numbering.  In DP-only mode DP owns both blocks.
+ * takes the other one: block B in normal, block A in reverse.  The DP PCS
+ * lane-pair selection (qmp_combo_configure_dp_mode()) has to follow the
+ * orientation as well, so dp_mode_ignore_reverse must stay clear on such a
+ * PHY.  In DP-only mode DP owns both blocks.
  */
 static void qmp_combo_dp_lane_blocks(struct qmp_combo *qmp, bool *use_tx,
 				     bool *use_tx2)
